```python
def unique_in_order(items):
    return sorted(set(items), key=lambda x: sorted(x, key=lambda x: x)))
```

This function uses the `sorted` and `set` method to remove duplicates while preserving the first-seen order. The time complexity is O(n log n) due to the sorting step.
